0:07:28Z"},"comments":21,"created_at":"2019-12-05T15:57:00Z","updated_at":"2022-01-21T19:02:39Z","closed_at":"2021-11-10T22:36:27Z","author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"When using a Python script in obs, loading a binary module fails due to non-exported CPython \r\nsymbols.\r\n\r\nI am using obs on a Linux Debian Buster.  Tested with obs compiled from current git master (ccb7d897) as well as the debian package provided in testing, aka  `obs-studio 24.0.3+dfsg1-2`.\r\n\r\nGiven the following example which tries to load the `termios` python package (a cython package):\r\n\r\n```python\r\nimport termios\r\n```\r\n## Expected Behavior\r\n\r\nI would expect this python snippet to load properly (and do nothing).\r\n\r\n## Current Behavior\r\n\r\nI fails with the following traceback:\r\n\r\n```\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\nFile \"/home/david/perso/elec/obs-tally/obsFirmataTally.py\", line 9, in <module>\r\n  import termios\r\nImportError: /usr/lib/python3.7/lib-dynload/termios.cpython-37m-x86_64-linux-gnu.so: undefined symbol: PyExc_TypeError\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Steps to Reproduce\r\n1. create a `test_import.py` script with the content being just `import termios`\r\n2. load the script in the Tools->Scripts dialog \r\n3. open the Script Log dialog to see the described  traceback\r\n\r\n## Additional information \r\n\r\nUsing Python 3.7 from the system (3.7.3-1).\r\n\r\nIt also fails to load numpy for example.","closed_by":{"login":"jp9000","id":2084112,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwODQxMTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2084112?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jp9000","html_url":"https://github.com/jp9000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jp9000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jp9000/